eholder\">\n          <span class=\"placeholder-label\">[Photograph]</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"person\">\n          <div class=\"person-name\">HUSSEIN ONN</div>\n          <p>Prime Minister of Malaysia<br>\n          Trained by the British army in Malaya,India,Middle-East<br>\n          Graduate from LINCOLN'S INN (London)</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"crime\">\n      <h2>PERPETRATORS OF CRIMES AGAINST THE<br>PEOPLE OF MALAYSIA AND SINGAPORE</h2>\n      <div class=\"crime-copy\">\n        <div class=\"intro\">To maintain the interests of British and other foreign capital<br>and the local elites, THEY</div>\n        <div>: SUPPRESS workers' and peasants' rights.</div>\n        <div>: BAN independent trade unions and student unions.</div>\n        <div>: MANIPULATE judicial process.</div>\n        <div>: SUPPRESS parliamentary democracy and press freedom.</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <h2 class=\"jail\">THEY JAIL AND KILL PEOPLE</h2>\n\n  <section class=\"connection\">\n    <h2>THE BRITISH CONNECTION</h2>\n    <div class=\"connection-subtitle\">\n      RUBBER AND TIN from colonial Malaya were crucial to British<br>\n      post-war recovery.\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"evidence\">\n      <div class=\"evidence-photo placeholder\">\n        <span class=\"placeholder-label\">[Photograph]</span>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"evidence-text\">\n        <p>\"Without Malaya, the Sterling System, as we know<br>\n        it, could not exist.\" Purcell</p>\n\n        <p>A 12-year British Military Rule was imposed after<br>\n        the World War II to protect British economic interests.</p>\n\n        <p>Repressive laws were first introduced by the British<br>\n        colonial regime, then further improved by the local<br>\n        elites.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"evidence-photo right placeholder\">\n        <span class=\"placeholder-label\">[Photograph]</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"influence\">\n      Though formally 'independent', Britain CONTINUES to exert influence<br>\n      and control through<br>\n      <div class=\"dash\">- &nbsp; Domination of the economies</div>\n      <div class=\"dash\">- &nbsp; Collaboration with the repressive regimes</div>\n      <div class=\"dash\">- &nbsp; Cultural subversion</div>\n      <div class=\"dash\">- &nbsp; Five-Power-Defence-Arrangement (U.K., Australia, New Zealand,<br>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Malaysia and Singapore).</div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"bottom-heading\">\n    <div>BELIEVED TO BE IN LONDON ATTENDING</div>\n    <div>THE COMMONWEALTH P.M. CONF.</div>\n    <div>JUNE 8-16,1977</div>\n  </section>\n\n  <div class=\"footer-note\">\n    Published by COBRA and NUS<br>\n    COBRA - Conference for Basic Human and Democratic Rights in the ASEAN alliance<br>\n    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;6, Endsleigh Street&nbsp;&nbsp;London WC1\n  </div>\n\n  <aside class=\"picket\">\n    <strong>LEE AND HUSSEIN ONN</strong><br>\n    Place: Parliament Square, London SW1<br>\n    Date: 10th June, 1977<br>\n    Time: 9 p.m.<br><br>\n    SEND LETTERS/TELEGRAMS of protest<br>\n    to Commonwealth Secretariat,<br>\n    Old? London Borough Houses,<br>\n    Copies to COBRA.\n  </aside>\n</main>\n</body>\n</html>"
